    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\nWhen attempting to synchronise after making changes to the file system in a directory managed by `markdown-oxide` LSP throws the following error:\n```\nE5108: Lua: ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2862: attempt to concatenate local 'scheme' (a userdata value)\nstack traceback:\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2862: in function 'is_scheme'\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2870: in function 'filt'\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2892: in function 'lsp_fs_hook_client'\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2853: in function 'lsp_fs_hook'\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2816: in function 'fs_actions_apply'\n        ...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:865: in function <...-repro/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:855>\n```\nThis appears to be caused by the LSP returning a value which Neovim's JSON decoder decodes as `vim.NIL`, which falls through to a `startswith` check. I was able to fix the issue locally by adding an additional type check to `is_scheme`.\n\n```lua\n-- mini.nvim/lua/mini/files.lua:2868\n-- before\nlocal is_scheme = function(uri, scheme) return scheme == nil or vim.startswith(uri, scheme .. ':') end\n\n-- after\nlocal is_scheme = function(uri, scheme) return scheme == nil or type(scheme) ~= 'string' or vim.startswith(uri, scheme .. ':') end\n```\n\nI'd be happy to open a PR to fix this myself if my proposed solution is satisfactory.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n1. Create separate 'nvim-repro' config directory:\n    - '~/.config/nvim-repro/' on Unix\n    - '~/AppData/Local/nvim-repro/' on Windows\n\n2. Inside 'nvim-repro' directory create a file named 'init.lua'.\n   Populate it with the following content:\n\n    ```lua\n    -- Clone latest 'mini.nvim' (requires Git CLI installed)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"Installing `mini.nvim`\" | redraw')\n    local mini_path = vim.fn.stdpath('data') .. '/site/pack/deps/start/mini.nvim'\n    local clone_cmd = { 'git', 'clone', '--depth=1', 'https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim', mini_path }\n    vim.fn.system(clone_cmd)\n    vim.cmd('echo \"`mini.nvim` is installed\" | redraw')\n\n    -- Make sure 'mini.nvim' is available\n    vim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\n\n    -- Extra steps\n    require('mini.files').setup({})\n\n    vim.lsp.enable({ 'markdown-oxide' })\n    ```\n    ```lua\n    -- nvim-repro/lsp/markdown-oxide.lua\n    return {\n        cmd = { 'markdown-oxide' },\n        filetypes = { 'markdown' },\n        root_markers = { '.moxide.toml', '.git' },\n    }\n    ```\n\n3. Run `NVIM_APPNAME=nvim-repro nvim` (i.e. execute `nvim` with `NVIM_APPNAME` environment variable set to \"nvim-repro\").\n   Wait for all dependencies to install.\n\n4. Create a directory with the following:\n  - an empty `.moxide.toml` file\n  - create two markdown files, `test1.md` and `test2.md`\n  - add a markdown link from one file to the other, e.g.\n```\n# test1.md\n[[test2]]\n```\n\n5. Open MiniFiles and attempt to add or delete a markdown note\n\n<details><summary>What to do after reporting an issue</summary>\n\nAfter reporting the issue, it is safe (and even recommended for cleaner possible future bug reports) to remove 'nvim-repro' config from the system:\n- Delete config directory ('~/.config/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete data directory ('~/.local/share/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n- Delete state directory ('~/.local/state/nvim-repro' on Unix).\n\n</details>\n",
